<title>UK: TENNIS-SEEDS UNDER PRESSURE AT WIMBLEDON.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-SEEDS UNDER PRESSURE AT WIMBLEDON.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>This year's Wimbledon fourth round</p>
<p>will feature the lowest number of women's seeds since the full</p>
<p>list of 16 was adopted in 1978.</p>
<p>The women's last 16 line-up contains just seven seeds, with</p>
<p>only three survivors from the top seven names on the original</p>
<p>list.</p>
<p>Amongst the men, the fall-out has been almost as severe with</p>
<p>just eight seeds taking their place in the fourth round.</p>
<p>In fact, this merely reflects the trend of recent years in</p>
<p>the men's event. There have been even fewer seeded</p>
<p>representatives at the same stage in each of the last three</p>
<p>years, even though Wimbledon is the only Grand Slam tournament</p>
<p>where seedings do not faithfully follow the world rankings.</p>
<p>The full fourth-round line-up (prefix number denotes</p>
<p>seeding):</p>
<p>Men's singles</p>
<p>1-Pete Sampras (U.S.) v 16-Petr Korda (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>9-Marcelo Rios (Chile) v 8-Boris Becker (Germany)</p>
<p>3-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) v Nicolas Kiefer (Germany)</p>
<p>12-Pat Rafter (Australia) v Todd Woodbridge (Australia)</p>
<p>Mark Woodforde (Australia) v Michael Stich (Germany)</p>
<p>14-Tim Henman (Britain) v 4-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands)</p>
<p>Greg Rusedski (Britain) v Richey Reneberg (U.S.)</p>
<p>Cedric Pioline (France) v Brett Steven (New Zealand)</p>
<p>Women's singles</p>
<p>1-Martina Hingis (Switzerland) v Sabine Appelmans (Belgium)</p>
<p>Maria Alejandra Vento (Venezuela) v Denisa Chladkova (Czech</p>
<p>Republic)</p>
<p>4-Iva Majoli (Croatia) v 12-Irina Spirlea (Romania)</p>
<p>Helena Sukova (Czech Republic) v Anna Kournikova (Russia)</p>
<p>Patricia Hy-Boulais (Canada) v Yayuk Basuki (Indonesia)</p>
<p>11-Mary Joe Fernandez (U.S.) v 3-Jana Novotna (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>8-Arantxa Sanchez Vicario (Spain) v 9-Mary Pierce (France)</p>
<p>Nathalie Tauziat (France) v Sandrine Testud (France)</p>
</text>
